WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.080
IELTS 17 published by Cambridge University Press and Assessment 2022. This recording is copyright.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:16.559
Test 1. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:16.559 --> 00:00:22.000
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.240
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:34.880
All the recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:41.840
you will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to the answer sheet. Now turn to part 1.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:53.840
Part 1. You will hear a woman called Jan phoning a man about their local conservation group.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.799
First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5.

00:01:23.839 --> 00:01:27.919
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.760
Of course. Well, we have a mixture of regular activities and special events.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.400
One of the regular ones is trying to keep the beach free of litter.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.759
A few of us spend a couple of hours a month on it and it's awful how much there is to clear.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:12.880
I wish people would be more responsible and take it home with them.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:19.440
I totally agree. I'd be happy to help with that. Is it OK to take dogs?

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.399
I'm afraid not as they're banned from the beach itself.

00:02:23.039 --> 00:02:26.800
You can take them along the cliffs though and children are welcome.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:27.119
Right.

00:02:27.919 --> 00:02:33.440
We also manage a nature reserve and there's a lot to do there all year round. For example,

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.399
because it's a popular place to visit, we spend a lot of time looking after the paths

00:02:38.399 --> 00:02:40.800
and making sure they're in good condition for walking.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.679
I could certainly help with that.

00:02:43.679 --> 00:02:47.759
Good. And we have a programme of creating new habitats there.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:52.720
We've just finished making and installing nesting boxes for birds to use

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.559
and next we're going to work on encouraging insects.

00:02:56.559 --> 00:02:59.600
They're important for the biodiversity of the reserve.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.039
They certainly are.

00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:06.320
Oh, and we're also running a project to identify the different species of butterflies

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:10.559
that visit the reserve. You might be interested in taking part in that.

00:03:10.559 --> 00:03:15.199
Sure. I was involved in something similar where I used to live,

00:03:15.199 --> 00:03:19.199
counting all the species of moths. I'd enjoy that.

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:23.919
Another job we're doing at the reserve is replacing the wall on the southern side

00:03:23.919 --> 00:03:29.759
between the parking area and our woodshed. It was badly damaged in a storm last month.

00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:30.259
OK.

00:03:33.759 --> 00:03:36.479
Before you hear the rest of the conversation,

00:03:36.479 --> 00:03:39.759
you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:41.059
OK.

00:04:05.039 --> 00:04:08.399
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.039
Then, as I said, we have a programme of events as well,

00:04:15.039 --> 00:04:17.679
both at the weekend and during the week.

00:04:17.679 --> 00:04:21.440
Right. I presume you have guided walks.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.480
I'd like to get to know the local countryside as I'm new to the area.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.519
Yes, we do. The next walk is to Ruston Island a week on Saturday.

00:04:31.519 --> 00:04:35.760
We'll be meeting in the car park at Dunsmore Beach at low tide.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.239
That's when the sands are dry enough for us to walk to the island without getting wet.

00:04:40.239 --> 00:04:41.040
Sounds good.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:47.600
The island's a great place to explore. It's quite small and it's got a range of habitats.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:53.279
It's also an ideal location for seeing seals just off the coast or even on the beach.

00:04:53.279 --> 00:04:59.279
OK. And is there anything we should bring, like a picnic for instance?

00:04:59.839 --> 00:05:02.799
Yes, do bring one as it's a full day walk.

00:05:03.519 --> 00:05:09.359
And of course it'll be wet walking across and back, so make sure your boots are waterproof.

00:05:09.359 --> 00:05:13.359
I must buy a new pair. There's a hole in one of my current ones.

00:05:14.239 --> 00:05:17.279
Well, I'd definitely like to come on the walk.

00:05:17.839 --> 00:05:23.920
Great. Then later this month we're having a one-day woodwork session in Hopton Wood.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:29.200
I've never tried that before. Is it OK for beginners to take part?

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.040
Definitely. There'll be a couple of experts leading the session

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.679
and we keep the number of participants down so you'll get as much help as you need.

00:05:37.679 --> 00:05:41.040
Excellent. I'd love to be able to make chairs.

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.480
That's probably too ambitious for one day. You'll be starting with wooden spoons

00:05:47.119 --> 00:05:53.200
and of course learning how to use the tools. And anything you make is yours to take home with you.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.480
That sounds like fun. When is it?

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:04.480
It's on the 17th from 10am until 3. There's a charge of £35 including lunch

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.000
or £40 if you want to camp in the wood.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:13.760
I should think I'll come home the same day. Well, I'd certainly like to join the group.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:25.279
That is the end of part one. You now have half a minute to check your answers to part one.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:36.480
You now have half a minute to check your answers to part one.

